{"url": "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/graduate-programs/tuition-scholarships-and-funding", "final_url": "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/graduate-programs/tuition-scholarships-and-funding", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-14", "text": "Skip to main content\nEnter your keywords\nSearchsearch\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nDepartments\nResearch\nIndustry & Community\nLife at CECS\nAlumni & Friends\nAbout\nUM-Dearborn Home\nStudent One-Stop\nFaculty & Staff\nCommunity & Business\nAlumni\nApply\nGiving\nBrowse A-Z\nBreadcrumb\nHome College of Engineering and Computer Science Graduate Programs Tuition, Scholarships, and Funding\nIN THIS SECTION\nGraduate Programs\nPhD and DEng Programs\nToggle Submenu\nMaster's Programs\nCertificates\nAdmissions\nToggle Submenu\nAdvising\nToggle Submenu\nTuition, Scholarships, and Funding\nProfessional Development Resources\nTuition, Scholarships, and Funding\nUM-Dearborn offers many sources of funding each year to assist students with their academic and living expenses. There are countless funding resources available from outside the university. Students are encouraged to actively research all applicable scholarship opportunities.\nTuition\nGet the information you need to calculate your tuition and fees, browse frequently asked questions, and find resources to pay for your graduate education.\nScholarships\nLearn more about scholarships available to new and current graduate students.\nInternal Funding Opportunities\nCECS Graduate Student Assistantships\nThe following funding opportunities exist for graduate students in CECS:\nGraduate Student Research Assistants (GSRA)\nGraduate Student Instructors (GSI)\nGraders\nTemporary employees\nGSI and GSRA funding opportunities are reserved for Ph.D. students. In some instances, opportunities may be available to master's level students. Individual faculty members and departments appoint GSRAs and GSIs. The opportunities for employment in each department vary each term.\nContact your department to learn more!\nComputer & Information Science\nMechanical Engineering\nIndustrial & Manufacturing Systems Engineering\nElectrical & Computer Engineering\nExternal Funding Opportunities\nThe following are external, non-University scholarship opportunities that may be of interest to University/CECS students. Inclusion of an external scholarship opportunity is intended only as a resource for students, and does not express or imply any University involvement with, or endorsement of, the external program.\nExternal Funding for Incoming and Current Graduate Students\nExternal Funding for Candidacy / Dissertation\nExternal Funding for International Students\nExternal Funding for Post-Doctoral\nCECS Graduate Education Office\nlinkedin\n2060/2070 - Professional Education Center\n4901 Evergreen Road\nDearborn, MI 48128\nView on Map\nSunday: Closed\nMonday: 8:00 am-5:00 pm\nTuesday: 8:00 am-5:00 pm\nWednesday: 8:00 am-5:00 pm\nThursday: 8:00 am-5:00 pm\nFriday: 8:00 am-5:00 pm\nSaturday: Closed\numd-engingrad@umich.edu\nDEARBORN\nFLINT\nANN ARBOR\n4901 Evergreen Rd\nDearborn, MI 48128, US\n313-593-5000\nContact us\nFacebook\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nX-Twitter\nYouTube\nMaps & Directions\nMy UM-Dearborn\nBookstore\nCanvas\nEmergency Information\nEmployment\nLibrary\nU-M Google Mail\nWolverine Access\n\u00a9 2026\nThe Regents of the University of Michigan Privacy Policy\n\" \"", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/graduate-programs/tuition-scholarships-and-funding#main"], ["", "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs"], ["Undergraduate Programs", "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/undergraduate-programs"], ["Majors and Minors", "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/undergraduate-programs/majors-and-minors"], ["Admissions", "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/undergraduate-programs/admissions"], ["Scholarships", "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/undergraduate-programs/scholarships"], ["International Studies", "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/undergraduate-programs/i